        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix visualizer coordinate and secure typing regressions",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- define one global CG/Accessibility-to-AppKit conversion boundary for visual feedback, capture selection, offscreen checks, and screen lookup\n- keep all visualizer geometry in logical points so Retina does not double-scale coordinates\n- retire stale per-screen element sheets, including an empty refreshed element map\n- sample secure focus before every text segment so typing captions stay masked after focus changes inside one action sequence\n- route macOS release credentials through the existing 1Password service-account item instead of interactive keychain/password prompts\n- update both changelogs and visualizer documentation\n\n## Root cause\n\nVisualizer inputs mixed global top-left CG/AX coordinates with bottom-left AppKit window coordinates. Individual call sites then flipped or scaled subsets of the data, which made window, element, mouse, and screen-selection paths disagree—especially on vertically arranged displays. Secure typing feedback also sampled focus too early or too late for multi-action input such as text, Tab, password text, Return.\n\n## Proof\n\n- `pnpm run format`\n- `pnpm run lint` — 0 serious findings; 19 pre-existing warnings\n- `pnpm run lint:docs`\n- `pnpm run test:safe` — 629 tests in 72 suites passed\n- focused Foundation geometry tests — 2/2 passed\n- focused screen-selection tests — 2/2 passed\n- focused visualizer overlay tests — 12/12 passed\n- focused secure-input tests — 6/6 passed\n- focused See visualizer tests — 4/4 passed\n- signed Debug Peekaboo 3.6.0 app built successfully with Xcode\n- candidate GUI bridge: Screen Recording, Accessibility, AppleScript, and event synthesis all granted\n- controlled Chrome target: AX click point `(2100,383)` exactly matched live overlay-window center `(2100,383)`\n- relocated anti-cheat target: click point `(2492,739)` exactly matched live overlay-window center `(2492,739)` at browser DPR 2\n- controlled synthetic password-field input reached the field while the live typing HUD rendered bullets only\n- candidate visualizer smoke: 15/15 event types dispatched, zero failures, live overlay windows present\n- black-box behavior contract: 3 pass, 0 fail, 0 blocked\n- fresh Codex autoreview: no actionable findings\n\nPhysical live proof used the currently attached single Retina display. Above-primary and below-primary layouts, overlap fallback, stale empty refresh, and logical-size preservation are covered by deterministic regression tests.\n\n## Risk\n\nModerate geometry surface area: capture, interaction feedback, screen selection, and visual overlays all consume the shared conversion. The conversion is deliberately point-only and reversible, with focused topology coverage and full-suite proof.\n",
